2026-09-24T02:01:57.2555155Z DiffWitness · Guided view — understand what changed, what is verified, and what needs attention
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2555418Z 
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2555510Z Start here:
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2555725Z   dw setup                           Connect DiffWitness to Claude/Codex/Cursor for this Git project
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2556168Z   dw status                          See what is known, unknown, and what to do next
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2556433Z After setup, use your coding agent normally; run `dw status` after a change.
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2556595Z 
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2556650Z Useful when needed:
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2556858Z   dw explain                         Explain the latest change from local evidence, with no AI required
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2557154Z   dw state why ID                     Find the recorded reasons and sources behind a memory item
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2557444Z   dw ask "question"                  Read cited project facts or an explicit abstention
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2557734Z   dw protect detect                  Check optional live protection without changing configuration
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2558023Z   dw view technical                  Open the complete engineering command surface
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2558177Z 
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2558298Z A blocked or observed runtime action is not proof that the final software works.
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2558653Z DiffWitness verifies the resulting Git change independently. Source code and raw prompts/diffs stay local by default.
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2558888Z 
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2559012Z For every command and advanced workflow: `dw view technical`, then `dw --help`.
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2559199Z 
2026-09-24T02:01:57.2559445Z Language: English by default. Save with `dw language en|fr`; override once with `dw --language en|fr <command>`. OS locale never selects product language.
